Below is a concise, ready‑to‑use list of the **long weekends** that occurred in Canada during 2023.  
A “long weekend” is defined as a three‑day stretch (Friday‑Sunday) that includes at least one public holiday.  
For holidays that fall on a weekend, the *observed* day (the nearest weekday) is used to create the long weekend.

| # | Holiday | Date (2023) | Observed (if weekend) | Long‑Weekend Span | Notes |
|---|---------|-------------|-----------------------|-------------------|-------|
| 1 | New Year’s Day | **Sunday, Jan 1** | Monday, Jan 2 | **Fri Dec 30 – Sun Jan 1** | 3 days off (Fri‑Sun) |
| 2 | Family Day (Alberta, BC, Saskatchewan, Ontario, etc.) | **Monday, Feb 20** | — | **Fri Feb 17 – Sun Feb 19** | 3 days off |
| 3 | Good Friday | **Friday, Apr 7** | — | **Fri Apr 7 – Sun Apr 9** | 3 days off |
| 4 | Victoria Day | **Monday, May 22** | — | **Fri May 20 – Sun May 22** | 3 days off |
| 5 | Canada Day | **Saturday, Jul 1** | Monday, Jul 3 | **Sat Jul 1 – Mon Jul 3** | 3 days off |
| 6 | Labour Day | **Monday, Sep 4** | — | **Fri Sep 2 – Sun Sep 4** | 3 days off |
| 7 | Thanksgiving | **Monday, Oct 9** | — | **Fri Oct 7 – Sun Oct 9** | 3 days off |
| 8 | Remembrance Day | **Saturday, Nov 11** | Monday, Nov 13 | **Sat Nov 11 – Mon Nov 13** | 3 days off |
| 9 | Christmas Day | **Monday, Dec 25** | — | **Fri Dec 23 – Sun Dec 25** | 3 days off |

